How to maintain this file
================================================================================

NOTICE is an Apache License 2.0 artifact: it carries attribution that must travel
with both source and binary distributions of this project. THIRD-PARTY is the
inventory of what we depend on; NOTICE is the legal attribution record.

Add an entry under "Attributions" when -- and only when -- at least one of the
following is true:

1. We modify third-party code licensed under Apache-2.0 and redistribute it.
   Section 4(b) of the license requires modified files to carry prominent
   notices stating that they were changed. Record the component, the files
   touched, and the nature of the change.
2. A third-party license requires its NOTICE text (or equivalent attribution) to
   be preserved in our distribution. Reproduce that text verbatim under
   "Attributions"; do not reword, summarize, or translate it.
3. We ship a component whose license obliges us to reproduce an attribution
   notice in a NOTICE / "about" surface (for example Apache-2.0 components that
   already have their own NOTICE file, or licenses with an attribution clause).

Do NOT add entries for:

- dependencies that never ship. Lint, test, and build-time tooling are inventoried
  in THIRD-PARTY under "Dev-only dependencies" instead; the authoritative list is
  devDependencies in package.json plus pnpm-lock.yaml.
- code we wrote, or first-party assets we created. Those are covered by the
  project copyright line above.

Keep every entry factual and minimal: component name, version, upstream URL,
license, and the exact obligation it satisfies. When an item fits both files,
record it in both.

